  "limitations": [
    "Test parent deliberately SIGKILLs only its authenticated qualification worker; there is no production fault switch.",
    "The killed process cannot emit a destructor/zero-owner receipt. Its exact process/service exit and startup fence were reconciled before replacement; the fresh worker emitted a zero-owner CUDA retirement receipt.",
    "The durable coordinator object was dropped and reopened; this does not qualify coordinator-process death or full Python controller/host-node recovery.",
    "Only one CUDA GPU and this mixed four-input fixture are covered. Broader failure boundaries, multiple GPUs, V100 and larger workloads remain open.",
    "No timing approval or throughput conclusion is drawn from this fault-injection run. The unchanged production CLI retains its separately recorded benchmark."
  ],
